  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Gunka are Japanese military and patriotic songs, begun in the Meiji era with pieces such as Battōtai, set by the French bandmaster Charles Leroux, and Setoguchi Tōkichi's Gunkan kōshinkyoku. Record companies issued them as wartime popular songs through the 1930s and early 1940s, among them Koseki Yūji's Roei no uta (1937), sung by solo singers or male groups over brass-led studio bands; the generic horn card stands in for the band's trumpets and trombones.",
